PE 854: Pisano Periods 2 / Pisano周期2

=== Problem Interpretation ===
Extended study of Pisano periods π(m).
May involve counting m with specific π(m) values,
or analyzing the distribution of Pisano periods.

=== Pisano Period Distribution (m ≤ 30) ===
π(m)  : m values
----------------------------------------
   1 : 1
   3 : 2
   6 : 4
   8 : 3
  10 : 11
  12 : 8
  14 : 29
  16 : 7 21
  18 : 19
  20 : 5
  24 : 6 9 12 16 18 24
  28 : 13
  30 : 22
  36 : 17
  40 : 15
  48 : 14 23 28
  60 : 10 20
  72 : 27
  84 : 26
 100 : 25
 120 : 30

=== Even Period Property ===
For m ≥ 3, π(m) is always even.
  m ≤ 10: 8/10 have even π(m)
  m ≤ 30: 28/30 have even π(m)
  m ≤ 50: 48/50 have even π(m)
  m ≤ 100: 98/100 have even π(m)

=== Fixed Points: π(m) = m ===
(Wall's conjecture: π(m)=m iff m=24·5^k)
  m = 1, π(1) = 1
  m = 24, π(24) = 24
  m = 120, π(120) = 120

=== Period Counts for Small Values ===
Observed Pisano period values for m ≤ 50:
